<p>Ukraine accused Russia of breaching Kyiv’s unilateral ceasefire after it took effect at midnight on May 6, saying attacks continued across Ukrainian territory even though Moscow had not accepted the proposal. The dispute followed separate, uncoordinated ceasefire announcements tied to Russia’s May 8-9 Victory Day commemorations: Putin ordered a two-day pause for those dates, while Zelenskyy announced an earlier Ukrainian “regime of silence” and urged Moscow to observe it. Kyiv said the continued fighting showed Russia had rejected the offer, while Russian officials made counter-accusations that left both unilateral truce claims disputed.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/_GV_iE8T7vVeKGW7LVhvb9aV2N_Zhu2i1Aa-xtZ4T8PTol2cc5-X6M0af_D7PcmjgjDzw2TpkUt75WYYK1Wa_9HXqPg0fjrsZmuHynij-dxhSJy70TFt3731YFfsT6XwjkbcwrnvcZBJFq8ncR0UCckcv3Y-ajd7HGuZ3d8QqMGpT4xedDj--SqsMtcmVxyhhlTKJ_lZBE93IDh47Z7Ck8ol5vBEuAA0kbj5MXaMl6-TyAA8xdHihW0A0do5EhJGdZEr' alt='Ukraine accused Moscow of violating a unilateral ceasefire declared by Kyiv.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Civilian sites: A Russian drone hit a kindergarten in northern Ukraine, and local authorities also reported damage in Zaporizhzhia, Sumy, Kharkiv and other regions.</li><li>Longer pause: Reports noted that Zelenskyy has repeatedly sought a prolonged ceasefire rather than a short halt around May 9.</li><li>Parade security: Moscow reinforced security measures ahead of its Victory Day military parade, according to Taz.</li><li>Battlefield fighting: Ukraine’s military reported ceasefire violations in the Pokrovsk area, while Zelenskyy listed continuing attacks in Donetsk, Kharkiv, Dnipro, Sumy, Chernihiv, Zaporizhzhia and Kherson.</li></ul><blockquote>We can confirm that the Russian side has derailed the ceasefire regime - Volodymyr Zelenskyy</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Volodymyr Zelenskyy: Zelenskyy said Ukraine would decide its further actions based on the situation overnight and the next day, and warned that Kyiv would respond symmetrically to Russian attacks. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/05/06/ukraine-will-respond-in-kind-zelenskyy-says-after-russia-breaks-kyivs-ceasefire'>Euronews</a>)</li><li>Andrii Sybiha: Ukraine’s foreign minister portrayed Moscow’s May 9 ceasefire proposal as a feigned pause unrelated to diplomacy, saying Putin was focused on military parades rather than human lives. (<a href='https://kurier.at/politik/ausland/drohnenangriffe-ukraine-russland-ignoriert-selenskijs-waffenruhe-vorstoss/403157298'>Kurier</a>)</li><li>Russian Defense Ministry: The ministry tied Russia’s ceasefire to Victory Day commemorations and warned of a massive strike on Kyiv if Ukraine tried to disrupt the Moscow parade. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/russia-derails-ceasefire-ukraine-will-act-in-kind-volodymyr-zelenskyy-said/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Russian authorities: Russian officials reported extensive Ukrainian drone attacks two days before Victory Day, challenging Kyiv’s assertion that only Moscow was violating ceasefire conditions. (<a href='https://www.bluewin.ch/de/news/international/moskau-meldet-ukrainische-angriffe-was-ist-mit-waffenruhe-3223047.html'>Bluewin</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/05/06/ukraine-will-respond-in-kind-zelenskyy-says-after-russia-breaks-kyivs-ceasefire'>’Ukraine will respond in kind’, Zelenskyy says after Russia breaks Kyiv’s ceasefire</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/ukraine-russia-kindegarten-drone-cease-fire-attacks-war/33751265.html'>Russian Drone Hits Ukrainian Kindergarten; Kyiv Accuses Moscow Of Flouting Cease-Fire</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1t5nhal/president_zelenskyy_announces_symmetrical/'>President Zelenskyy Announces Symmetrical Response to Russian Ceasefire Violations</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://meduza.io/en/feature/2026/05/06/russia-ukraine-victory-day-truce-collapse